  "domain": "artificial-intelligence",
  "definition": "Privacy-Utility Tradeoffs represent the fundamental tension in privacy-preserving AI between privacy preservation\u2014protecting sensitive information through techniques such as differential privacy, anonymisation, or encryption\u2014and model utility, which encompasses accuracy and other performance metrics necessary for effective decision-making. This tension is characterised by Pareto frontiers of achievable (privacy, utility) pairs where strengthening privacy typically degrades model performance and vice versa.",
